=== meta ===
rule: BROAD_EXCEPT_ADDED
title: `self.assertTrue(True, "first", "second")` in a `unittest.TestCase` handler raises TypeError, so the handler does not swallow
origin: #496, a negative for R49's first condition: the call may pass only the method's operands and at most one literal `msg`
note: broad_except_always_passing_unittest_pos with one more positional argument; `assertTrue(expr, msg=None)` takes two, so the call fails whatever its operand is; app.py is unchanged and outside the diff
=== before: tests/test_value.py ===
import unittest

from app import value


class ValueTest(unittest.TestCase):
    def test_value(self):
        self.assertEqual(value(), 1)
=== after: tests/test_value.py ===
import unittest

from app import value


class ValueTest(unittest.TestCase):
    def test_value(self):
        try:
            self.assertEqual(value(), 1)
        except Exception:
            self.assertTrue(True, "first", "second")
